:: Racecourse
<<effects>>
<<run setup.horserace.ensureState()>><<run setup.horserace.weeklyState()>><<outfitChecks>>
<<if $farm.horseRaceUnlocked isnot true>>
	The fenced-off course is quiet. Alex has not opened it for racing yet.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif $daily.horseRaceCancelled>>
	<<endevent>>
	<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
	The course is empty. A steward is taking the numbers down off the betting board while two
	of the bookies pack their slips away.
	<br><br>
	Alex is standing by the rail with <<his>> arms folded. "They've called off the whole meeting,"
	<<he>> says. "Someone was interfering with the runners, and once the stewards say that out loud nobody will take a bet."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> looks at the empty course for a moment, then back at you. "<span class="pink">We try again tomorrow.</span>"
	<br><br>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if $horserace.phase is "idle" or $horserace.phase is "finished" or $horserace.phase is "closed">><<run setup.horserace.createRace(true)>><</if>>
	<<if $horserace.phase is "closed">>
		<<endevent>>
		<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
		The racecourse is much quieter than usual. A few handlers linger near the stable gate,
		but no bookies are calling odds and no horses are being led to the start.
		<br><br>
		Alex checks the empty course, then gives you an apologetic look.
		"The horses don't look in any shape to run today. Too many are lame or shaken up. We'll have to close betting until they're right again.
		<span class="pink">Maybe we can train them better...</span>"
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		The racecourse is already noisy. Bookies shout over each other, betting slips pass from hand to hand,
		and the horses are led towards the gate.
		<br><br>
		<<if $weekly.horseRaceIncidentLossStreak gte 2>>
			<span class="purple">A strange hesitation sits under the noise today</span>.
			A few handlers watch the runners too closely, and some of the bookies lower their voices before taking the next slip.
			No one says the race is fixed, but no one looks comfortable either.
		<</if>>
		<<if $exposed gte 2>>
			<span class="pink">A few conversations die as you approach</span>.
			The bookies stare, the handlers pretend not to, and Alex quickly steps closer as if <<nnpc_he "Alex">>
			can block the whole racecourse from seeing you.<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
			<<if $face isnot "covered">><<fameexhibitionism 8>><</if>>
		<<elseif $exposed is 1>>
			<span class="pink">Several people glance your way and whisper</span>,
			but the bookies are more interested in taking bets than asking questions about what you're wearing...
			or almost not wearing.<<garousal>><<arousal 200>>
		<</if>>
		<<print setup.horserace.renderHorseList()>>
		<<link "Place a bet" "Racecourse Betting">><</link>>
		<br>
		<<if $horserace.phase is "betting">>
			<<if $horserace.rigEntered>>
				<<link "Stable yard" "Racecourse Rigging">><</link>>
			<<else>>
				<<link "Stable yard" "Racecourse Rigging Enter">><</link>>
			<</if>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<br>
		<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Betting
<<effects>>
<<if $horserace.phase is "closed">>
	<<endevent>>
	<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
	<<if $horserace.riggedCancelled>>
		Alex lowers <<his>> voice. "They've pulled the race. Something about the betting pattern looked off.
		<span class="pink">We should let it cool down before trying again.</span>"
	<<else>>
		Alex gives the empty course another look. "The horses don't look in any shape to run today.
		Too many are lame or shaken up. We'll have to close betting until they're right again.
		<span class="pink">Maybe we can train them better...</span>"
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif setup.horserace.atWeeklyWinCap()>>
	You turn towards the betting window before stopping. There are far more people here, somehow...
	<br><br>
	Seems word has got round about the run you have had, and half the town has come to try the same thing.
	At each bookie, there is a stagnant line packed with at least twenty people.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Push into the queue|Racecourse Crowded Push]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Go back|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	The board changes one last time while the bookie calls for final bets.
	<<print setup.horserace.renderHorseList()>>
	<<if !$horserace.selectedHorseId>>
		Choose a horse to back.
		<p class="horse-race-bet-links">
		<<set _firstHorseLink to true>>
		<<for _horse range $horserace.horses>>
			<<if _firstHorseLink>><<set _firstHorseLink to false>><<else>><br><</if>>
			<<set _label to _horse.name + " (" + _horse.odds.toFixed(2) + "x)">>
			<<capture _horse>>
				<<link _label "Racecourse Betting">><<set $horserace.selectedHorseId to _horse.id>><<set $horserace.betInput to "">><</link>>
			<</capture>>
		<</for>>
		</p>
	<<else>>
		<<set _horse to setup.horserace.getHorse($horserace.selectedHorseId)>>
		You choose <<print _horse.name>>. Choose how much you want to bet.
		<<set _presetBets to [100, 500, 1000, 2000]>><<set _firstBet to true>><<set _shownPreset to false>>
		<p class="horse-race-bet-links">
		<<for _amount range _presetBets>>
			<<set _internalAmount to setup.horserace.toInternalMoney(_amount)>>
			<<if $money >= _internalAmount>>
				<<set _shownPreset to true>>
				<<if _firstBet>>
					<<set _firstBet to false>>
				<<else>>
					 |
				<</if>>
				<<set _label to _amount.toLocaleString("en-GB") + "£">>
				<<capture _amount>>
					<<link _label "Racecourse Betting Submit">><<set $horserace.betInput to _amount + "">><</link>>
				<</capture>>
			<</if>>
		<</for>>
		</p>
		<<if !_shownPreset>>
			<span class="red">You do not have enough money for the smallest preset bet.</span>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<steedicon>><<link "Choose a different horse" "Racecourse Betting">><<set $horserace.selectedHorseId to "">><<set $horserace.betInput to "">><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Crowded Push
<<effects>>
You turn sideways and push your shoulder into a small gap between two people.
They shift for you to squeeze through, letting you move a few places closer to the betting window.
Yet the gap quickly closes behind you.
<br><br>
More people press in from both sides, forcing you to slow down and move with the queue instead of passing through it.
<br><br>
An elbow hits you hard in the ribs as someone tries to make room. You flinch and grab your side,
but the crowd is packed too tightly for anyone to stop or turn around.<<gpain>><<pain 4>><<gstress>><<stress 6>>
<br><br>
You look ahead. There are still several rows of people between you and the betting window.
<br><br>
<<link [[Keep pushing|Racecourse Crowded Push Two]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Go back|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Racecourse Crowded Push Two
<<effects>>
You push forward again and manage another two steps before everyone suddenly stops.
You nearly walk into the person in front of you.
<br><br>
<<generate1>><<person1>>
A steward stands on a crate near the betting board, waving both arms and shouting for everyone
behind the barrier to move back. The command just makes the crowd pack in tighter as everyone fights
to keep their spot.
<br><br>
You try to squeeze past the <<person>> in front of you, but <<he>> blocks the gap. Upon your next try, <<he>> flattens <<his>>
hand against your chest to shove you back a step, keeping <<his>> back turned the entire time.
<br><br>
You stumble into the person behind you and quickly catch your balance.<<ggpain>><<pain 8>><<ggstress>><<stress 12>>
<br><br>
There is no way through. The betting window is still buried behind the crowd,
with too many people ahead of you to reach it in time. You turn sideways and slowly work your way
back through the queue until you finally reach open space, then leave the racecourse behind.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Racecourse Betting Submit
<<set _betResult to setup.horserace.placeBet($horserace.selectedHorseId, $horserace.betInput)>>
<<if _betResult.ok>>
	The bookie takes your stake, tears off a betting slip, and waves you towards the rail.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Go to the viewing rail|Racecourse Rail Check]]>><<npc Alex>><<person1>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if $horserace.lastError>><p class="red"><<print $horserace.lastError>></p><</if>>
	<<link [[Return to the betting window|Racecourse Betting]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Racecourse Rail Check
<<outfitChecks>><<npc Alex>><<person1>>
<<if $horserace.phase is "betting">>
	The race can't start until you place a bet.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the betting window|Racecourse Betting]]>><</link>>
<<elseif $exposed gte 2 and $settings.horsesEnabled and $daily.horseRaceHorseBreakChecked isnot true>>
	<<set $daily.horseRaceHorseBreakChecked to true>><<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>><<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>>
	Several horses glance your way as you approach the viewing rail. At first, it is easy to blame the noise, the crowd, or the unfamiliar scent of the racecourse.
	Then you notice how fixed their attention is. Their ears turn towards you. One of them stops listening to its handler entirely.
	<br><br>
	<span class="pink">Only then does your own nakedness feel impossible to ignore.</span>
	<br><br>
	Alex notices, then looks you over with a frown. "Why are you walking around dressed like that here?"
	<br><br>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek">>
		"Sorry," you say quietly, drawing in on yourself. "I didn't think it would matter."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		"It's not your business," you mutter, glancing aside.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
		"I don't think my clothes are the important part right now, Alex," you say.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
		"I can move away from the rail if you want," you say.
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel")>>
		"None of your business," you say.
		<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
			You make no effort to hide your irritation.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		"It's not your business," you say.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Alex opens <<his>> mouth, then stops as a few spectators nearby snicker.
	"Fine," <<he>> says, clicking <<his>> tongue. "Wear whatever you want at the biggest horse race we've ever had. Brilliant idea."
	<br><br>
	The horse that has been staring at you suddenly jerks hard against its lead. Its handler swears, boots sliding in the dirt as the animal surges towards the rail.
	Alex tries to grab you, but the crowd panics and shoves between you.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Racecourse Horse Break]]>><<endevent>><<beastNEWinit 1 horse>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>
<<else>>
	One of the horses glances your way as you reach the viewing rail, then another. A third starts shifting uneasily, tugging at its lead until the handler has to pull it back.
	<br><br>
	One of the handlers hauls a horse back before it can get too close to the rail. Alex goes pale. "Maybe don't stand too close," <<he>> says, keeping one eye on the horses.<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Watch the race|Racecourse Watch]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Watch
<<outfitChecks>>
<<if $horserace.phase is "betting">>
	The race can't start until you place a bet.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the betting window|Racecourse Betting]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<print setup.horserace.renderTrack()>>
	<<script>>setTimeout(function () {setup.horserace.placeMarkers(); setup.horserace.refreshLiveView("Racecourse Result", "See the result");}, 0);<</script>>
	<<print setup.horserace.renderRaceLog()>>
	<<print setup.horserace.renderLiveControls("Racecourse Result", "See the result", "Start watching", "Pause watching", 1600)>>
	<span id="horse-race-result-link">
	<<link "Skip to the finish" "Racecourse Result">><<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>><<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>><</link>>
	</span>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Result
<<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>><<endevent>>
<<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>>
<<if $horserace.phase isnot "finished">><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>><</if>>
<<print setup.horserace.renderResult()>>
<<link "Run another race" "Racecourse Betting">><<run setup.horserace.createRace(true)>><</link>>
<<if $horserace.lossTraumaPending>><<gggtrauma>><<trauma 15>><<set $horserace.lossTraumaPending to false>>
<<elseif $horserace.lossStressPending>><<gggstress>><<stress 20>><<set $horserace.lossStressPending to false>><</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<run setup.horserace.clearRaceData()>><</link>>

:: Racecourse Horse Break
<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>
	<<beastNEWinit 1 horse m penis beast>>
	<<beastCombatInit>>
	<<set $NPCList[0].stance to "top">>
	<<if $pronoun is "m">>
		<<set $position to "doggy">>
	<<else>>
		<<set $position to "missionary">>
	<</if>>
	<<set $position_lock to 1>>
<</if>>
<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<beast $enemyno>>
<<audience>>
<<stateman>>
<<actionsman>>
<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Racecourse Horse Break Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Racecourse Horse Break]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Horse Break Finish
<<effects>>
The handlers finally get the horse under control and drag it away from the rail. The crowd takes a long moment to settle, muttering and staring as the bookies shout for everyone to move back.
<br><br>
By the time Alex finds you again, the race has already finished.
<br><br>
<<endcombat>>
<<link [[Next|Racecourse Result]]>><</link>>

:: Farm Horse Race Intro
<<run setup.horserace.ensureState()>>
<<set $farm.horseRaceUnlocked to true>><<set $farm.horseRaceIntroSeen to true>>
Alex leads you past the stable, down a fresh line of fencing where the grass has been cut short and the mud has been packed flat. Workers are still arguing over posts near the far bend, but the shape of the place is clear already: a racecourse.
<br><br>
"I wanted to show you before anyone else saw it," Alex says, unable to hide <<his>> smile. "We've done well. Not just survived. Done well. And that's because of you. The fields, the animals, the repairs... all of it. I couldn't have got this far alone."
<br><br>
<<He>> rubs the back of <<his>> neck. "One of my dad's old business partners helps run race meetings. Transport, bookies, safety checks, all that boring official stuff. We got talking, and... well. They're willing to work with us. We provide the land and horses. They bring the people who know how to make it legal and profitable."
<br><br>
A board has been nailed near the gate. The paint is still drying.
<br><br>
<span class="gold">Alex's farm can now host horse races.</span>
<br><br>
"No pressure," Alex adds, badly pretending this isn't the most excited <<he>> has looked all week. "But I thought we could walk the course. Make sure it doesn't fall apart before I invite half the town here."
<br><br>
<<link [[Walk the course|Farm Horse Race Walk]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Farm Horse Race Walk
<<effects>>
One of the race horses stamps as you pass, neck arched and ears flicking. Its handler murmurs to it, but the horse looks more interested in the open track than in behaving.
<br><br>
"See? That's what I mean. Farm horses want a job. Race horses want a reason to bolt, and we just try to make sure they bolt in the right direction." <<He>> clicks <<his>> tongue as the horse tosses its head. "Still easier than dealing with Remy. Usually."
<br><br>
<<if $settings.bestialityEnabled>>
	One stallion near the rail goes still as you pass, ears forward and body tense, before becoming <span class="pink">far too obviously excited, its cock visibly erect</span>.
	Another horse at the far end gives you the same fixed stare. Then a third.
	<br><br>
	Alex follows your gaze, then notices another horse reacting the same way. His face turns scarlet. "Right... Brilliant. Great. We're going over there now."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> catches your sleeve and quickly ushers you away from the rail, putting <<himself>> between you and the horses.
<<else>>
	One stallion near the rail goes very still as you pass, ears forward and body tense. It stamps once, then twice, making Alex wince.
	Another horse at the far end starts making a fuss. Then a third joins in, tugging at its lead until the handler has to calm it down.
	<br><br>
	Alex looks from one horse to the next, frowning. "Right... Brilliant. Great. We're going over there now."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> catches your sleeve and quickly ushers you away from the rail.
<</if>>
<br><br>
By the viewing rail, the handlers are already lining the horses up.
"Let's watch them once," Alex says. "If nobody panics, jumps a fence, or makes me regret this, I'll call it a success."
<br><br>
<<link [[Watch the trial race|Farm Horse Race Trial Watch]]>><<run setup.horserace.startTrialRace()>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Farm Horse Race Trial Watch
<<print setup.horserace.renderTrack()>>
<<script>>setTimeout(function () {setup.horserace.placeMarkers(); setup.horserace.refreshLiveView("Farm Horse Race Trial Result", "See how it went");}, 0);<</script>>
<<print setup.horserace.renderRaceLog()>>
<<print setup.horserace.renderLiveControls("Farm Horse Race Trial Result", "See how it went", "Start the trial race", "Pause watching", 1600)>>
<span id="horse-race-result-link">
<<link "Let Alex skip to the finish" "Farm Horse Race Trial Result">><<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>><<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>><</link>>
</span>

:: Farm Horse Race Trial Result
<<set $horserace.autoWatch to false>>
<<run setup.horserace.cancelAutoWatch()>>
<<if $horserace.phase isnot "finished">><<run setup.horserace.simulateToEnd(false)>><</if>>
<<print setup.horserace.renderResult()>>
Alex watches the winner by the far rail. Only then does <<he>> seem to remember how to breathe. "Nothing broke!" <<He>> laughs, still a little nervous. "I'll take that as a good sign."
<br><br>
A handler waves from the track. Alex waves back, then turns to you with a brighter smile.
<br><br>
"I'll have the betting board ready next time," <<he>> says. "Come back when you want to watch a proper race. The bookies should be ready by then, if you feel like risking a little cash."
<br><br>
<span class="gold">The racecourse is now open from the farmyard.</span>
<br>
<<link [[Return to the farm|Farm Work]]>><<endevent>><<run setup.horserace.clearRaceData()>><</link>>

:: Racecourse Rigging Enter
<<effects>>
<<if $horserace.phase isnot "betting">>
	The moment has passed. The horses are already at the start.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the racecourse|Racecourse]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set $horserace.rigEntered to true>>
	<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
	"I'm going to go look at the horses before they line up," you say.
	<br><br>
	Alex is still watching the betting board, one hand on the rail. "Want me to come? I know most of the handlers."
	<br><br>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<if _speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy">>
		"It's fine," you say. "I won't be long."
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
		"I can walk down a path on my own," you say.
	<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant">>
		"Stay and watch the odds for me," you say. "Tell me if they move."
	<<else>>
		"Someone should keep an eye on the board," you say. "I'll be back before the off."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<He>> shrugs, then turns back to the board.
	<br><br>
	You leave the crowd behind and walk down the slope towards the farm.
	The shouting from the bookies grows quieter as you reach the yard.
	A steward waits beside the gate with a clipboard. <<He>> checks the list when you approach,
	finds your name, then steps aside to let you through. No questions are needed. You are with the farm.
	<br><br>
	You enter the yard. Two rows of stalls run along either side of a wide dirt path. Handlers move between them,
	bringing water, checking equipment, and leading horses out one at a time. Ahead of you,
	another runner is being taken towards the course.
	<br><br>
	You watch it leave through the far gate. Once the final horse is taken out, betting closes.
	If you plan to do anything before the race, you need to do it now.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Racecourse Rigging]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Rigging
<<effects>>
<<if $horserace.phase isnot "betting">>
	The moment has passed. The horses are already at the start.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the racecourse|Racecourse]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<generate1>><<person1>>
	<<if $horserace.suspicion is 0>>
		The yard is busy with the usual work. Handlers carry feed, check tack,
		and move between the stalls without paying you any attention.
	<<elseif $horserace.suspicion lt 30>>
		You pass a handler carrying a bucket. <<He>> gives you a quick nod before continuing towards the stalls.
		Nobody else seems interested in what you are doing.
	<<elseif $horserace.suspicion lt 60>>
		A steward enters through the yard gate and starts checking the stalls one by one.
		<<He>> speaks briefly with each handler before moving on. There are still several horses between <<him>> and you.
	<<elseif $horserace.suspicion lt 80>>
		The steward reaches the end of the row and stops there. <<He>> looks towards you several times
		while pretending to check the nearby stalls. Two handlers beside the water trough begin talking quietly,
		and one keeps looking in your direction.
	<<else>>
		<span class="red">Three officials are waiting by the yard gate.</span> One of them checks a
		betting sheet while another points towards your end of the stalls. When you look over, none of them turns away.
	<</if>>
	<<endevent>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $horserace.suspicion gte 1>>
		<span class="orange">Suspicion: <<print $horserace.suspicion>>%.</span>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<span class="teal">Chance your horse finishes the race without being pulled up: <<print setup.horserace.cleanRunChance()>>%.</span>
	<br><br>
	<<set _tierColours to { high: "purple", medium: "pink", low: "blue" }>>
	<<set _tierLabels to { high: "High risk", medium: "Medium risk", low: "Low risk" }>>
	<<for _action range setup.horserace.RIG_ACTIONS>>
		<<if _action.deviancyGated and !(hasSexStat("deviancy", 2) and $settings.horsesEnabled and $settings.bestialityEnabled)>>
			<<continue>>
		<</if>>
		<<set _used to setup.horserace.rigActionUsed(_action.id)>>
		<<set _colour to _tierColours[_action.tier]>>
		<<if _used>>
			<<crimeicon>><span class="grey"><<print _action.label>></span>
		<<elseif _action.cost and $money < setup.horserace.rigCostInternal(_action)>>
			<<crimeicon>><span class="grey"><<print _action.label>></span> |<span class="red"> Need <<print setup.horserace.formatMoney(setup.horserace.rigCostInternal(_action))>></span>
		<<elseif _action.itemCost is "phial" and $phials_stored < 1>>
			<<crimeicon>><span class="grey"><<print _action.label>></span> |<span class="red"> Need a phial</span>
		<<else>>
			<<crimeicon>><<capture _action>>
				<<link _action.label "Racecourse Rigging Target">><<set $horserace.rigActionId to _action.id>><</link>>
			<</capture>>
			<<if _action.deviancyGated>><<deviant2>><</if>>
			|<span @class="_colour"> <<print _tierLabels[_action.tier]>></span><<if _action.cost>> <</if>><<if _action.itemCost is "phial">> <span class="grey">1 phial</span><</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<</for>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Back to the rail|Racecourse Rigging Leave]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Rigging Leave
<<effects>>
<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
You head back up the slope while the last runners are led out of the yard towards the course.
<<if $horserace.suspicion is 0>>
	Alex is still by the rail, checking the board when you return. <<He>> looks over as you stop beside <<him>>.
	"Anything worth knowing?"
	<br><br>
	"They all look fine to me," you say.
	<br><br>
	Alex gives a small nod and turns back to the board.
<<elseif $horserace.suspicion lt 40>>
	Alex looks over as you come back to the rail. "You were down there a while."
	<br><br>
	"I was looking at the horses," you say.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> watches you briefly, then turns back to the board without asking anything else.
<<elseif $horserace.suspicion lt 70>>
	When you reach the rail, Alex is watching the yard gate instead of the board.
	"A steward went in after you. Came back out and went straight to the officials' tent."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> looks at you, waiting for an explanation. You keep quiet and turn your attention towards the course.
	<<gstress>><<stress 6>>
<<else>>
	Alex grabs your arm as soon as you reach the rail and pulls you closer. "What did you do?
	They've had three people out of that yard in the last ten minutes. Now they're all gathered around the board."
	<br><br>
	You look over. Several officials are talking beside it, while two of the bookies have stopped taking bets.
	<br><br> <span class="red">Something has clearly gone wrong.</span><<ggstress>><<stress 14>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Racecourse]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Racecourse Rigging Target
<<effects>>
<<set _action to setup.horserace.getRigAction($horserace.rigActionId)>>
<<if !_action or $horserace.phase isnot "betting">>
	<<link [[Return to the racecourse|Racecourse]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if _action.target is "own">>
		Which horse do you want to help?
	<<else>>
		Which horse do you want to target?
	<</if>>
	<br>
	<<for _horse range $horserace.horses>>
		<<capture _horse>>
			<<capture _action>>
				<<link _horse.name _action.passage>><<set $horserace.rigTargetId to _horse.id>><</link>>
			<</capture>>
		<</capture>>
		<br>
	<</for>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Never mind|Racecourse Rigging]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Rig Minigame
<<effects>>
<<set _game to setup.horserace.rigGameState()>>
<<set _action to setup.horserace.getRigAction(_game.actionId)>>
<<set _horse to setup.horserace.getHorse($horserace.rigTargetId)>>
<<if !_action or !_horse or $horserace.phase isnot "betting">>
	<<link [[Return to the racecourse|Racecourse]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<set _text to setup.horserace.RIG_MINIGAME_TEXT[_game.actionId]>>
	<<print _text.scene>>
	<<print setup.horserace.renderRigMeters()>>
	<<crimeicon>><<link _text.quick "Racecourse Rig Minigame Step">><<set $horserace.rigGame.pendingMode to "quick">><</link>> | <span class="red">Risky</span>
	<br>
	<<crimeicon>><<link _text.careful "Racecourse Rig Minigame Step">><<set $horserace.rigGame.pendingMode to "careful">><</link>> | <span class="teal">Slow</span>
	<br>
	<<investigateicon>><<link _text.watchLabel "Racecourse Rig Minigame Step">><<set $horserace.rigGame.pendingMode to "watch">><</link>> | <span class="blue">Lowers risk</span>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Rig Minigame Step
<<effects>>
<<set _game to setup.horserace.rigGameState()>>
<<set _action to setup.horserace.getRigAction(_game.actionId)>>
<<set _horse to setup.horserace.getHorse($horserace.rigTargetId)>>
<<set _text to setup.horserace.RIG_MINIGAME_TEXT[_game.actionId]>>
<<set _mode to _game.pendingMode>>
<<set _success to true>>
<<if _mode isnot "watch">>
	<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to setup.horserace.rigMinigameDifficulty(_action, _mode)>>
	<<skulduggerycheck "silent">>
	<<set _success to $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
<</if>>
<<run setup.horserace.applyMinigameTurn(_mode, _success)>>
<<set _outcome to setup.horserace.rigMinigameOutcome()>>
<<if _mode is "quick">>
	<<print _success ? _text.quickSuccess : _text.quickFail>>
<<elseif _mode is "careful">>
	<<print _success ? _text.carefulSuccess : _text.carefulFail>>
<<else>>
	<<print _text.watch>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _outcome is "ongoing">>
	<<link [[Continue|Racecourse Rig Minigame]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _outcome is "success">>
	<<link "Next" $horserace.rigSuccessPassage>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link "Next" $horserace.rigCaughtPassage>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Rig Injure Horse
<<effects>>
<<set _horse to setup.horserace.getHorse($horserace.rigTargetId)>>
<<if !_horse or $horserace.phase isnot "betting">>
	<<link [[Return to the racecourse|Racecourse]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<endevent>>
	<<generate1>><<person1>>
	You walk along the stable row until you find <<print _horse.name>> tied outside its stall.
	Its handler, a <<person>>, is further down the row, busy checking another horse's tack.
	<br><br>
	You crouch beside <<print _horse.name>>'s front leg and place your hand around the edge of the shoe.
	The horse shifts its weight, forcing you to wait until it stands still again.
	You start pulling at the shoe, trying to loosen it enough to cause trouble once the race begins.
	<br><br>
	<<set $horserace.rigSuccessPassage to "Racecourse Rig Injure Horse Success">>
	<<set $horserace.rigCaughtPassage to "Racecourse Rig Injure Horse Caught">>
	<<run setup.horserace.startRigMinigame("injure_horse")>>
	<<link [[Start|Racecourse Rig Minigame]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Racecourse Rig Injure Horse Success
<<effects>>
<<set _horse to setup.horserace.getHorse($horserace.rigTargetId)>>
The nail comes loose under your fingers. You push it back into the hole just far enough to keep the shoe in place,
then lower the hoof and step away before anyone notices.
<br><br>
<span class="pink">The shoe looks secure, but it will come loose once <<print _horse.name>> starts running.</span>
<<run setup.horserace.resolveRigAction("injure_horse", _horse.id, true)>>
<br><br>
<<riggingFooter>>

:: Racecourse Rig Injure Horse Caught
<<effects>>
<<set _horse to setup.horserace.getHorse($horserace.rigTargetId)>>
The handler comes back down the row and sees you crouched by the horse's leg.
<br><br>
"Hey! Get away from that horse!" <<he>> shouts, closing the distance fast and grabbing your arm.
<<gpain>><<pain 3>>
<br><br>
<<if $athletics gte 400>>
	<<link "Pull free" "Racecourse Rig Injure Horse Escape">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link "Run" "Racecourse Rig Injure Horse Run">><</link>>
<br>
<<link "Talk" "Racecourse Rig Injure Horse Talk">><</link>>

:: Racecourse Rig Injure Horse Escape
<<effects>>
<<set _horse to setup.horserace.getHorse($horserace.rigTargetId)>>
You pull your arm free before <<he>> can get a proper hold on you.
<<He>> reaches for your clothes, but you slip out of reach and hurry towards the gate without looking back.
<br><br>
<<He>> does not chase you. By the time you leave the yard, <<he>> has already turned back to check the horse's leg.
<br><br>
<<set $horserace.suspicion to Math.min(100, $horserace.suspicion + 8)>>
<<run setup.horserace.resolveRigAction("injure_horse", _horse.id, false)>>
<<riggingFooter>>

:: Racecourse Rig Injure Horse Run
<<effects>>
<<set _horse to setup.horserace.getHorse($horserace.rigTargetId)>>
You pull against <<his>> grip, but <<he>> keeps hold of your arm and tries to drag you back.
You wrench your arm sideways until <<his>> hand slips free, then turn and run for the gate.
<br><br>
You keep running until you are out of the yard. Only then do you slow down and glance back.
<br><br>
Your shoulder hurts where <<he>> grabbed you.<<gpain>><<pain 3>><<gstress>><<stress 4>>
<br><br>
<<set $horserace.suspicion to Math.min(100, $horserace.suspicion + 15)>>
<<run setup.horserace.resolveRigAction("injure_horse", _horse.id, false)>>
<<riggingFooter>>

